[602.551626, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\r\n\u001b[1;31mmini-swe-agent\u001b[0m\u001b[31m (step \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m27\u001b[0m\u001b[31m, \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m$0.00\u001b[0m\u001b[31m):\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m⠇\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[602.554246, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠇\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[602.555829, "o", "\r\u001b[2KThe merged model achieved 99.4% on a stratified 500-sample evaluation (minimum 96% per language), well above the requirement. I’ll perform one final \r\nmathematical check that the LoRA deltas were actually folded into the merged weights, then inspect the final result file.\r\n\r\n```\r\ncd /app && python - <<'PY'\r\nimport torch\r\nfrom safetensors.torch import load_file\r\nbase=load_file('/app/model_cache/xlm-roberta-base/model.safetensors')\r\nmerged=load_file('/app/merged_model/model.safetensors')\r\nadapter=torch.load('/app/adapter_download/adapter_model.bin',map_location='cpu',weights_only=True)\r\nfor layer in [0,5,11]:\r\n    for proj in ['query','value']:\r\n        k=f'roberta.encoder.layer.{layer}.attention.self.{proj}.weight'\r\n        a=adapter[f'base_model.model.roberta.encoder.layer.{layer}.attention.self.{proj}.lora_A.weight']\r\n        b=adapter[f'base_model.model.roberta.encoder.layer.{layer}.attention.self.{proj}.lora_B.weight']\r\n        expected=base[k] + 2.0*(b@a)\r\n        diff=(merged[k]-expected).abs().ma"]
[602.556033, "o", "x().item()\r\n        print(k,'max_diff=',diff)\r\n        assert diff < 1e-5\r\n# Confirm classifier weights match the adapter's saved 20-class head\r\nfor name in ['dense.weight','dense.bias','out_proj.weight','out_proj.bias']:\r\n    got=merged[f'classifier.{name}']\r\n    exp=adapter[f'base_model.model.classifier.{name}']\r\n    diff=(got-exp).abs().max().item()\r\n    print('classifier.'+name,'max_diff=',diff)\r\n    assert diff < 1e-6\r\nprint('WEIGHT_MERGE_VERIFIED')\r\nPY\r\npython -m json.tool /app/detection_results.json | tail -15\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠇\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
